{"pudding":{"id":"2025697b-a9ea-4e2f-8031-d1d430b1a622","word":"pudding","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"sausage made primarily from blood","tags":["feminine"],"word":"morcela"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"boiled or steamed cake or dessert","tags":["masculine"],"word":"pudim"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"dessert similar to custard or mousse, containing a starchy thickening agent","tags":["masculine"],"word":"pudim"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The dishes in this chapter represent a range of multiethnic savory custards and steamed puddings, including a few surprises like a chèvre popover pudding and a bread pudding with lettuce and cheese.","ref":"2004, Victoria Wise, The Pressure Cooker Gourmet, page 313:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[88,95],[88,96],[146,153],[166,173]],"id":"a41ecf2a-9f7e-4b16-9921-4b52300d5a5f"},{"text":"Steamed and boiled puddings have formed the basic diet of country people in northern Europe for centuries. Early puddings consisted of the scoured stomach of a sheep or pig, stuffed with its own suet and offal, which has been thickened with oatmeal, and boiled in water or baked in the ashes of a fire.","ref":"2004, Sarah Garland, The Complete Book of Herbs & Spices, page 199:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[19,27],[113,121]],"id":"b8366a72-eb6d-448b-909a-1545ef373da7"}],"links":[["sweet","sweet"],["savoury","savoury"],["boiling","boiling"],["steaming","steaming"],["batter","batter"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Any of various dishes, sweet or savoury, prepared by boiling or steaming, or from batter."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"cd175311-803e-4f2f-b812-0158e60ce6e4"},{"examples":[{"text":"Steamed puddings, a favourite for winter, are both easy to make and delicious. Served with one of the sweet sauces (recipes 497 to 506) they make a filling and satisfying end to a meal.","ref":"2007, Magdaleen Van Wyk, The Complete South African Cookbook, page 265:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[8,16]],"id":"785066f4-aee4-4818-b88c-46e394fa73a6"}],"links":[["cake","cake"],["dessert","dessert"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["A type of cake or dessert cooked usually by boiling or steaming."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"d737c998-acd5-47d2-9f99-4577d886bb3a"},{"links":[["dessert","dessert"],["custard","custard"],["mousse","mousse"]],"hyponyms":[{"word":"custard"},{"word":"crème caramel"},{"word":"crème brûlée"},{"word":"flan"},{"word":"mousse"}],"glosses":["A type of dessert that has a texture similar to custard or mousse but using some kind of starch as the thickening agent."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"e8d01912-5dc1-4524-b08c-03ab2ed95379"},{"examples":[{"text":"We have apple pie for pudding today.","bold_text_offsets":[[22,29]],"type":"example","id":"dc55e882-fb31-4065-b769-fa50c95f8bbb"}],"categories":["Australian English","British English","English terms with usage examples","New Zealand English"],"links":[["Dessert","dessert"],["course","course"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"afters","tags":["UK","informal"]},{"word":"dessert"},{"word":"pud","tags":["UK","slang"]},{"word":"sweet","tags":["UK"]}],"raw_glosses":["(UK, Australia, New Zealand) Dessert; the dessert course of a meal."],"glosses":["Dessert; the dessert course of a meal."],"tags":["Australia","New-Zealand","UK","countable","uncountable"],"id":"3767b987-e8fa-4420-8e18-f0c317af6393"},{"links":[["sausage","sausage"],["blood","blood"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"black pudding","tags":["Ireland","UK"]},{"word":"blood sausage"}],"raw_glosses":["(originally) A sausage made primarily from blood."],"qualifier":"originally","glosses":["A sausage made primarily from blood."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"ce9eaf68-a289-43ef-b4c9-73f2d202cdd2"},{"categories":["English slang"],"links":[["overweight","overweight"]],"synonyms