ages with 5 entries","Pages with entries","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Hungarian translations","Terms with Latin translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Spanish translations"],"glosses":["An appropriate sense of modesty or shame."],"tags":["uncountable"],"id":"c6887fc2-40c5-4a83-a3bc-e92078f699c0"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Puducherry":{"id":"f381f590-26ef-407b-9c1f-09906fb71d4f","word":"Puducherry","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Puducherry, India","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Pondicherry"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["en:Places in India","en:Puducherry, India","en:States and union territories of India"],"links":[["union territory","union territory"],["India","India#English"],["exclave","exclave"],["capital","capital"],["Karaikal","Karaikal"],["Yanam","Yanam"],["Mahe","Mahe"]],"glosses":["A union territory in southern India, consisting of four geographically separated exclaves of former French India, namely its capital, Karaikal, Yanam, and Mahe."],"id":"4fd7fa65-a27d-4649-8c68-b6d2c3f7474b"},{"categories":["en:Cities in India","en:Cities in Puducherry, India","en:Places in India","en:Places in Puducherry, India","en:Puducherry","en:Territorial capitals of India"],"links":[["capital city","capital city"],["Puducherry","Puducherry#English"],["India","India#English"]],"glosses":["The capital city of the union territory of Puducherry, India."],"id":"d087aac0-97de-4b46-8fae-0f798806bf0b"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"word":"Pondicherry"}]},"puddle":{"id":"d0160aa1-b9f6-430e-8f78-e6b1659791bd","word":"puddle","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a small pool of water","tags":["feminine"],"word":"poça"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Foꝛ with the only be theſe welles of lyfe, / Of frayle men ſpring but podels of myꝛe, / From whom ſourdeth errour ⁊ croked ſtrife[…]","ref":"1560, “Pſalme. xxxvi”, in Matthew Parker, The whole Pſalter tranſlated into Engliſh metre […] , Iohn Daye, page 98:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[70,76]],"id":"9a59dcb3-bbe1-40cf-a1c7-26108aa992be"}],"attestations":[{"date":"from 14th c.","references":[]}],"links":[["pool","pool"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["A small, often temporary, pool of water, usually on a path or road."],"id":"3cc93fae-cddc-4e97-ac2a-ee158ae323ba"},{"examples":[{"text":"And fast beside a little brooke did pas / Of muddie water, that like puddle stank […].","ref":"1596, Edmund Spenser, “Book IV, Canto V”, in The Faerie Queene. […], London: […] [John Wolfe] for William Ponsonbie, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[69,75]],"id":"59185611-3a93-4d06-a416-e4b810d9efb9"},{"text":"searching their habitations for water, we could fill but three barricoes, and that such puddle, that never till then we ever knew the want of good water.","ref":"1624, John Smith, Generall Historie, Kupperman, published 1988, page 90:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[88,94]],"id":"b334b713-3927-4987-8ce1-aa40c35cd344"}],"attestations":[{"date":"from 16th c.","references":[]}],"categories":["English dialectal terms","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["Stagnant","stagnant"],["water","water"]],"raw_glosses":["(now dialectal) Stagnant or polluted water."],"glosses":["Stagnant or polluted water."],"tags":["dialectal"],"id":"0384434f-0799-4b20-a0ee-8859fe02ce3b"},{"attestations":[{"date":"from 18th c.","references":[]}],"links":[["homogeneous","homogeneous"],["clay","clay"],["grit","grit"],["canal","canal"],["pond","pond"],["watertight","watertight"]],"glosses":["A homogeneous mixture of clay, water, and sometimes grit, used to line a canal or pond to make it watertight."],"id":"82b3129a-047b-4eed-9722-1745dfe00aef"},{"examples":[{"text":"I had only to see the 'puddle' to know that your paddle made it.","ref":"1969, Charles Cuthbert Brown, Malay Sayings, page 88:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[22,29]],"id":"e597cebe-0e07-4314-ace7-ca52440e2091"},{"text":"As the blade exits the water the puddle is very tight and dark. It is also very quiet.","ref":"2007, Rowing News, volume 14, number 5, page 36:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[33,39]],"id":"8e7bd9d0-2b0d-4816-8da4-1a68679a7131"}],"topics":["hobbies","lifestyle","rowing","sports"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned","en:Rowing"],"links":[["rowing","rowing#Noun"],["ripple","ripple"],["oar","oar"]],"raw_glosses":["(rowing) The ripple left by the withdrawal of an oar from the water."],"glosses":["The ripple left by the withdrawal of an oar from the water."],"id":"67a54307-67ae-4fe1-8f14-b350f8d75e1a"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]}}
